@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000

### Health check
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/health

### Role-gate check — no session cookie, expect 401 UNAUTHENTICATED
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/recipes

### Auth

### 1. Register
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "testuser",
  "email": "test@neorecipe.com",
  "password": "securepassword123"
}

### 2. Login
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "test@neorecipe.com",
  "password": "securepassword123"
}

### 3. Get Me
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me

### 4. Logout
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/logout

### 5. Fetch Recipes after Logout (role-gate check — expect 401 UNAUTHENTICATED)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/recipes

###############################################################################
# Recipe CRUD — the write path (POST / GET-one / PUT / DELETE + image upload)
#
# Run these IN ORDER. The Sprint 3 blocks further down assume a real recipe
# exists, and this is what creates one.
#
# Image uploads need a real file on disk. The `< ./path` syntax below is the
# REST Client multipart file-reference form — put a small .jpg at
# docs/fixtures/sample.jpg (not committed) or repoint the path at any local image.
###############################################################################

@userAEmail = chef-a@neorecipe.com
@userBEmail = chef-b@neorecipe.com
@testPassword = securepassword123

### W1. Register user A (skip if already registered — expect 409 in that case)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "chefa",
  "email": "{{userAEmail}}",
  "password": "{{testPassword}}"
}

### W2. Register user B — needed for the 403 ownership checks
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "chefb",
  "email": "{{userBEmail}}",
  "password": "{{testPassword}}"
}

### W3. Log in as user A — sets the session cookie for everything below
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{userAEmail}}",
  "password": "{{testPassword}}"
}

### W4. Upload an image on its own — expect 201 { data: { url } }
###     The multipart field name MUST be `image` (API_CONTRACT.md § File Uploads).
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/uploads
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=NeoRecipeBoundary

--NeoRecipeBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="image"; filename="sample.jpg"
Content-Type: image/jpeg

< ./fixtures/sample.jpg
--NeoRecipeBoundary--

### W5. Upload rejects a non-image — expect 400 VALIDATION_ERROR
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/uploads
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=NeoRecipeBoundary

--NeoRecipeBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="image"; filename="notes.txt"
Content-Type: text/plain

not an image
--NeoRecipeBoundary--

### W6. CREATE a recipe — multipart: recipe fields + the `image` file.
###     `ingredients` and `steps` are JSON STRINGS in a single field each.
###     Expect 201 { data: { recipe } } with author = user A, set from the
###     session. Copy the returned _id into @newRecipeId below.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/recipes
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=NeoRecipeBoundary

--NeoRecipeBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="title"

Creamy Garlic Parmesan Pasta
--NeoRecipeBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="description"

A quick one-pot pasta tossed in a rich garlic parmesan sauce.
--NeoRecipeBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="category"

food
--NeoRecipeBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="prepTimeMinutes"

10
--NeoRecipeBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="servings"

4
--NeoRecipeBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="ingredients"

[{"name":"Spaghetti","quantity":"200 g"},{"name":"Garlic","quantity":"4 cloves"},{"name":"Parmesan cheese","quantity":"50 g"}]
--NeoRecipeBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="steps"

["Cook the spaghetti.","Saute the garlic in butter.","Toss with parmesan."]
--NeoRecipeBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="image"; filename="sample.jpg"
Content-Type: image/jpeg

< ./fixtures/sample.jpg
--NeoRecipeBoundary--

### W6b. CREATE a recipe WITH NO IMAGE — the `image` file is optional on create
###      (docs/API_CONTRACT.md § File Uploads). Expect 201 { data: { recipe } }
###      with imageUrl: null. No "image" part is included at all below.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/recipes
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=NeoRecipeBoundary

--NeoRecipeBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="title"

Recipe With No Photo
--NeoRecipeBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="description"

Verifies POST /api/recipes succeeds with no image file attached.
--NeoRecipeBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="category"

food
--NeoRecipeBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="prepTimeMinutes"

5
--NeoRecipeBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="servings"

1
--NeoRecipeBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="ingredients"

[{"name":"Salt","quantity":"1 pinch"}]
--NeoRecipeBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="steps"

["Nothing to see here."]
--NeoRecipeBoundary--

### W7. AUTHOR CANNOT BE SPOOFED — same as W6 but with an `author` field in the
###     body. Expect 201, and the returned author is still user A, NOT the id
###     sent here. Identity comes from the JWT only (CLAUDE.md §9).
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/recipes
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=NeoRecipeBoundary

--NeoRecipeBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="title"

Author Spoof Attempt
--NeoRecipeBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="description"

The author field below must be ignored by the server.
--NeoRecipeBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="category"

food
--NeoRecipeBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="prepTimeMinutes"

5
--NeoRecipeBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="servings"

1
--NeoRecipeBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="ingredients"

[{"name":"Salt","quantity":"1 pinch"}]
--NeoRecipeBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="steps"

["Do nothing."]
--NeoRecipeBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="author"

000000000000000000000000
--NeoRecipeBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="image"; filename="sample.jpg"
Content-Type: image/jpeg

< ./fixtures/sample.jpg
--NeoRecipeBoundary--

### W8. Create with a bad category — expect 400 VALIDATION_ERROR
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/recipes
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=NeoRecipeBoundary

--NeoRecipeBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="title"

Bad Category
--NeoRecipeBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="description"

Should be rejected.
--NeoRecipeBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="category"

drinks
--NeoRecipeBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="prepTimeMinutes"

5
--NeoRecipeBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="servings"

1
--NeoRecipeBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="ingredients"

[{"name":"Salt","quantity":"1 pinch"}]
--NeoRecipeBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="steps"

["Nothing."]
--NeoRecipeBoundary--

### W9. Create with malformed ingredients JSON — expect 400 VALIDATION_ERROR
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/recipes
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=NeoRecipeBoundary

--NeoRecipeBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="title"

Broken Ingredients
--NeoRecipeBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="description"

Should be rejected, not 500.
--NeoRecipeBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="category"

food
--NeoRecipeBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="prepTimeMinutes"

5
--NeoRecipeBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="servings"

1
--NeoRecipeBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="ingredients"

[{broken json
--NeoRecipeBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="steps"

["Nothing."]
--NeoRecipeBoundary--

### ---- Paste the _id returned by W6 here before continuing ----
@newRecipeId = PASTE_THE_W6_RECIPE_ID_HERE

### W10. GET one by id — expect 200 { data: { recipe } }, author { _id, username }
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/recipes/{{newRecipeId}}

### W11. GET a well-formed but nonexistent id — expect 404 NOT_FOUND
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/recipes/000000000000000000000000

### W12. GET a malformed id — expect 404 NOT_FOUND (not a 500 CastError)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/recipes/not-an-objectid

### W13. EDIT own recipe — JSON, not multipart. Partial update. Expect 200.
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/recipes/{{newRecipeId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Creamy Garlic Parmesan Pasta (updated)",
  "servings": 6
}

### W14. Edit with an empty body — expect 400 VALIDATION_ERROR
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/recipes/{{newRecipeId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### W15. Rating fields are not client-writable — expect 200, but averageRating
###      and ratingCount are stripped, not applied. Follow with W10 to confirm
###      they still hold whatever the rating endpoint set.
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/recipes/{{newRecipeId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Rating spoof attempt",
  "averageRating": 5,
  "ratingCount": 999
}

### W16. OWNERSHIP — log in as user B, then run W17/W18. Expect 403, not 401:
###      user B IS authenticated, just not the author.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{userBEmail}}",
  "password": "{{testPassword}}"
}

### W17. Edit a recipe owned by user A, as user B — expect 403 FORBIDDEN
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/recipes/{{newRecipeId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "user B must not be able to do this"
}

### W18. Delete a recipe owned by user A, as user B — expect 403 FORBIDDEN
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/recipes/{{newRecipeId}}

### W19. Log back in as user A (the owner) to finish the chain
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{userAEmail}}",
  "password": "{{testPassword}}"
}

### W20. DELETE own recipe — expect 204 No Content
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/recipes/{{newRecipeId}}

### W21. Confirm it is gone — expect 404 NOT_FOUND
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/recipes/{{newRecipeId}}

### W22. Role gate — run Logout first, then each of W22-W26 must be 401.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/uploads

### W23. Create with no session — expect 401 UNAUTHENTICATED
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/recipes

### W24. Get one with no session — expect 401 UNAUTHENTICATED
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/recipes/{{newRecipeId}}

### W25. Edit with no session — expect 401, NOT 403 (identity is unknown)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/recipes/{{newRecipeId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "no session"
}

### W26. Delete with no session — expect 401 UNAUTHENTICATED
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/recipes/{{newRecipeId}}


###############################################################################
# Sprint 3 — Signal + Discovery
#
# Ordering matters. Run the Auth block above first to get a session cookie, and
# set @recipeId below to a real recipe _id from the "List all recipes" call.
# The two-user rating checks need a SECOND account — register/login as user B
# where marked, then come back.
###############################################################################

@recipeId = PASTE_A_REAL_RECIPE_ID_HERE
@commentId = PASTE_A_REAL_COMMENT_ID_HERE

### Search / Filter / Sort ####################################################

### S1. List all recipes — no params, expect 200 { data: { recipes: [...] } }
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/recipes

### S2. Search by recipe title — expect only titles matching "pasta"
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/recipes?search=pasta

### S3. Search by INGREDIENT name — "garlic" is an ingredient, not a title word.
###     Expect the garlic-containing recipe back. This is the title-OR-ingredient case.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/recipes?search=garlic

### S4. Search with a regex metacharacter — must NOT 500.
###     Expect 200 with an empty or literal-match list, never a server error.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/recipes?search=C%2B%2B

### S5. Filter by category=food — expect only category "food"
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/recipes?category=food

### S6. Filter by category=bakery — expect only category "bakery"
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/recipes?category=bakery

### S7. Invalid category — expect 400 VALIDATION_ERROR
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/recipes?category=drinks

### S8. Sort by top — expect descending averageRating
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/recipes?sort=top

### S9. Sort by new — expect descending createdAt (newest first)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/recipes?sort=new

### S10. Invalid sort — expect 400 VALIDATION_ERROR
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/recipes?sort=oldest

### S11. Combined search + category + sort
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/recipes?search=a&category=food&sort=top

### Comments ##################################################################

### C1. Create a comment — body field is `body` (DATA_SHAPES.md), expect 201
###     { data: { comment } } with author { _id, username }.
###     Copy the returned _id into @commentId above.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/recipes/{{recipeId}}/comments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "body": "Made this last night — the garlic butter step is the whole trick."
}

### C2. List comments — expect 200 { data: { comments: [...] } } including C1's
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/recipes/{{recipeId}}/comments

### C3. Empty body — expect 400 VALIDATION_ERROR
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/recipes/{{recipeId}}/comments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "body": "   "
}

### C4. Wrong field name (`text` instead of `body`) — expect 400 VALIDATION_ERROR.
###     Guards the CLAUDE.md §11 regression.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/recipes/{{recipeId}}/comments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "text": "this should be rejected"
}

### C5. Comment on a nonexistent recipe — expect 404 NOT_FOUND
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/recipes/000000000000000000000000/comments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "body": "no such recipe"
}

### C6. Delete OWN comment — expect 204 No Content
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/comments/{{commentId}}

### C7. Ownership check — 403, NOT 401.
###     Steps: as user A, run C1 and copy the new comment _id into @commentId.
###     Then log in as user B (Auth block, different account) and run this.
###     Expect 403 FORBIDDEN — user B is authenticated, just not the author.
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/comments/{{commentId}}

### C8. Delete with no session at all — expect 401 UNAUTHENTICATED.
###     Run Logout first. 401 vs 403 must not be conflated.
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/comments/{{commentId}}

### Ratings ###################################################################

### R1. Rate 4 — expect 200 { data: { rating } } with value 4.
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/recipes/{{recipeId}}/rating
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "value": 4
}

### R2. Confirm the write landed — expect averageRating 4, ratingCount 1
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/recipes?search=

### R3. IDEMPOTENCY — same user re-rates 2. Expect 200, and the rating REPLACED.
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/recipes/{{recipeId}}/rating
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "value": 2
}

### R4. Verify replace-not-append — expect ratingCount STILL 1, averageRating 2.
###     If ratingCount is 2 here, the upsert is appending and the test has failed.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/recipes

### R5. TWO-USER AVERAGE — log in as user B, then rate the same recipe 5.
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/recipes/{{recipeId}}/rating
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "value": 5
}

### R6. Hand-computed check — user A left 2, user B left 5.
###     Expect ratingCount 2 and averageRating (2 + 5) / 2 = 3.5
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/recipes

### R7. Out-of-range low — expect 400 VALIDATION_ERROR
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/recipes/{{recipeId}}/rating
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "value": 0
}

### R8. Out-of-range high — expect 400 VALIDATION_ERROR
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/recipes/{{recipeId}}/rating
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "value": 6
}

### R9. Non-integer — expect 400 VALIDATION_ERROR
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/recipes/{{recipeId}}/rating
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "value": 3.5
}

### R10. Rating a nonexistent recipe — expect 404 NOT_FOUND
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/recipes/000000000000000000000000/rating
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "value": 3
}

### Role gate #################################################################

### G1. Run Logout first, then each of these must return 401 UNAUTHENTICATED.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/recipes?search=pasta

### G2. Comments list with no session — expect 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/recipes/{{recipeId}}/comments

### G3. Rating with no session — expect 401
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/recipes/{{recipeId}}/rating
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "value": 3
}
